Lots of script bugs due to parameters to commands not being set.
They would be easier to detect by using this shell feature:
${parameter:?word} prints a message including word if word is not null
and exits a non-interactive shell if parameter is unset or null.

echo ${pa:?}
bash: pa: parameter null or not set

When building software, resolve missing libraries by installing their -dev package,
runtime package is not sufficient.

scp globbing, use single quotes to stop local shell filename substitution:
scp 'ctap@lux.physics.albany.edu:/media/ctap/BENCAM-COPY/PP-2025-01-30/N*.mp4' .

